      "# POPCORN — evidence before a deadline or handoff\n\nHave your agent go to https://767-2676.com/agent-entry.\n\nNeed another participant to check when an exact task digest was presented?\nPOPCORN signs that digest and a witnessed time interval. Keep task contents local.\nUse it when a deadline matters or approved work passes to another agent.\nTime is evidence. The task owner and executor retain permission and enforcement.\n\n",
      "# Verify a checkpoint against two independent witnesses.\n\nKeep a FreeTSA RFC 3161 timestamp and a POPCORN receipt for the same SHA-256 digest; verify each in its native format. Preserve the exact checkpoint bytes with both proofs.\n\nLooking for an RFC 3161 timestamp authority, proof of existence, or trusted timestamping? Compare FreeTSA, OpenTimestamps, and POPCORN: https://767-2676.com/prove-action-before-authorization-expired\n\nPOPCORN uses its own signed receipt protocol; it is not an RFC 3161 timestamp authority. Its time interval is issuer-asserted. The task owner and executor retain permission and enforcement; the receipt does not prove identity, authorization, delivery, or execution.\n\nAgent entry and existing POPCORN verification samples: https://767-2676.com/agent-entry\n\n"
