    if (url.pathname === "/pricing") { return withDiscoveryHeaders(discoveryDocumentResponse(request, "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Pricing | 767-2676.com</title><style>:root{color-scheme:dark}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0b3d2e;color:#f2efe3;font:18px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}main{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:44px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-2px}h2{font-size:24px;margin-top:36px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #718b7f}code{font-size:.85em}nav{margin-top:40px;font:14px monospace}header a{text-decoration:none}</style></head><body><main><header><a href=\"/\">767-2676.com</a></header><h1>Pricing</h1><p>0.001 USDC per signed response, paid through x402 on Base.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Signed time<br><code>GET /v1/time</code></td><td>0.001 USDC</td></tr><tr><td>Digest witness<br><code>POST /v2/receipt</code></td><td>0.001 USDC</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Public documentation, verification keys, and saved examples are free to read. You can hash your own bytes and verify a saved receipt locally without payment.</p><p>An unpaid request to either paid endpoint returns the payment requirements. Check the amount, network, asset, and recipient before authorizing payment.</p><p><a href=\"/agent/offer\">Read the service offer</a> · <a href=\"/openapi.json\">Read the API contract</a></p><nav><a href=\"/agents\">agents</a> · <a href=\"/pricing\">pricing</a> · <a href=\"/terms\">terms</a></nav></main></body></html>\n", "text/html; charset=utf-8")); }
    if (url.pathname === "/terms") { return withDiscoveryHeaders(discoveryDocumentResponse(request, "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Service terms | 767-2676.com</title><style>:root{color-scheme:dark}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0b3d2e;color:#f2efe3;font:18px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}main{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:44px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-2px}h2{font-size:24px;margin-top:36px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #718b7f}code{font-size:.85em}nav{margin-top:40px;font:14px monospace}header a{text-decoration:none}</style></head><body><main><header><a href=\"/\">767-2676.com</a></header><h1>Service terms</h1><p>767-2676.com provides signed temporal evidence. These terms describe the scope published in its service offer and witness protocol.</p><h2>What you receive</h2><p>A signed time response states the service’s time and validity window. A digest witness records when the supplied SHA-256 commitment was presented, together with the submitted nonce and optional predecessor digest.</p><h2>Your data</h2><p>Keep the original task and schedule bytes with you. The witness endpoint accepts the digest and the fields defined by its request schema. It rejects additional fields.</p><h2>Payment</h2><p>Each signed time response or digest witness costs 0.001 USDC on Base through x402. Read the current payment challenge before authorizing a payment. Public documentation, verification keys, and saved examples are free to read.</p><h2>Using the evidence</h2><p>Verify the signature, expected digest, nonce, predecessor where applicable, and time window before relying on a response. Apply your own task authority and boundary conditions. The signed scope covers temporal evidence; identity, authorization, execution, delivery, and outcome require their own evidence.</p><p>Network delay and clock uncertainty remain part of verification. A saved sample retains its original timestamp and validity window.</p><p><a href=\"/agent/offer\">Service offer</a> · <a href=\"/schemas/witness-request.v1.json\">Request schema</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/violetclaire/popcorn-temporal-anchor/blob/main/docs/WITNESS_PROTOCOL.md\">Witness protocol</a></p><nav><a href=\"/agents\">agents</a> · <a href=\"/pricing\">pricing</a> · <a href=\"/terms\">terms</a> · <a href=\"/privacy\">privacy</a></nav></main></body></html>\n", "text/html; charset=utf-8")); }
    if (url.pathname === "/tone-spec.v1.json") { return withDiscoveryHeaders(discoveryDocumentResponse(request, "{\n  \"spec\": \"767-2676-tone-plan\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"quadrantTone\": {\n    \"waveform\": \"sine\",\n    \"durationMs\": 1200,\n    \"attackMs\": 40,\n    \"releaseMs\": 100,\n    \"autoplay\": false\n  },\n  \"boxes\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"NEED\",\n      \"question\": \"What has to happen?\",\n      \"frequencyHz\": 350\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"YES\",\n      \"question\": \"What has to remain true for you to proceed?\",\n      \"frequencyHz\": 440\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"BOUNDARY\",\n      \"question\": \"What turns YES into NO?\",\n      \"frequencyHz\": 480\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"TIME\",\n      \"question\": \"When does that boundary occur?\",\n      \"frequencyHz\": 620\n    }\n  ],\n  \"signals\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"GO_AHEAD\",\n      \"frequenciesHz\": [\n        350,\n        440\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"WAITING\",\n      \"frequenciesHz\": [\n        440,\n        480\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"NO\",\n      \"frequenciesHz\": [\n        480,\n        620\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"PROCEED\",\n      \"frequenciesHz\": [\n        1000\n      ],\n      \"durationMs\": 800,\n      \"waveform\": \"sine\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changePolicy\": \"Any change to a box frequency or signal frequency mapping requires a new spec version.\"\n}\r\n", "application/json; charset=utf-8")); }
    if (url.pathname === "/signal.md") { return withDiscoveryHeaders(discoveryDocumentResponse(request, "# 767-2676.com signal mapping\nSpec: 767-2676-tone-plan\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nGO_AHEAD = 350 + 440 Hz\nWAITING = 440 + 480 Hz\nNO = 480 + 620 Hz\nPROCEED = 1000 Hz; sine wave; 800 ms; single tone, never a chord.\n\nThe first three pairs use the component frequencies of North American dial, ringback, and busy tones respectively. Historical telephone signals also depend on cadence; the pairs alone do not specify a complete telephone signal.\n\nThe 1000 Hz / 800 ms PROCEED mapping is this site's chosen reference signal. Playing a tone does not create a signed witness or establish authorization. This file documents the signal mapping; it does not implement a decision endpoint.\n\nFront-page tones:\nNEED = 350 Hz\nYES = 440 Hz\nBOUNDARY = 480 Hz\nTIME = 620 Hz\n\nEach heading plays its single sine-wave frequency for 1200 ms, with a 40 ms attack and 100 ms release. Playback requires a tap, click, or keyboard activation. No autoplay.\n\nThe visible frequency, data-frequency-hz, and llms.txt mapping must agree. Agents can read the values without processing audio.\n\nAny change to a frequency or signal mapping requires a new specification version. The former 220/330/440/660 preview values were unversioned draft choices.\n\r\n", "text/markdown; charset=utf-8")); }
